  "goodToKnow": "Kuppeln means to couple (railway carriages) and, when driving, to use the clutch: kuppeln und schalten. Die Kupplung is the clutch or coupling. Learning to drive in Germany usually means a manual car; a licence obtained in an automatic used to be restricted, though the rules were relaxed in 2021. Verkuppeln means to matchmake: Sie will mich mit ihrem Cousin verkuppeln. Die Kuppel (dome) is different. Regular: kuppelte, gekuppelt."
